---
/**
 * What every verdict carries. Four properties of the decision form, each with a
 * line copied verbatim from a run:
 *
 *   examined  qcl_qcm_freeze         check_decomposable, Vacuous
 *   margin    qcl_geometric_qec      the LDPC bound that is too tight
 *   path      qcl_code_switching     the composition law names its norm
 *   refusal   qcl_concatenated_code  the gate across code blocks
 *
 * Two properties that need no output line follow as sentences: the tolerances
 * derive from the working type, and the compiler orders validate before control.
 */
import OutputCard from '../shared/OutputCard.astro';

const props = [
  {
    kind: 'Examined',
    title: 'Every check counts what it examined.',
    text: 'A check that examined nothing reads Vacuous, so an empty pass cannot pass for evidence. A two-node chain has no C₃ sub-relation (the pattern two commuting CNOTs create), so the decomposability check has nothing to search and says so.',
    out: `check_decomposable   Vacuous  examined 0  worst margin 0.000e0`,
  },
  {
    kind: 'Margin',
    title: 'Rejections name the offender.',
    text: 'Each check reports its measurement, its threshold and their ratio, the margin. A weight bound of 3 fails the toric code at its first Z check, where the weight is 4.',
    out: `bound 3: rejected at (Z, Column(0)) with margin 1.333 after 1 items`,
  },
  {
    kind: 'Path',
    title: 'Reports say exact or numeric.',
    text: 'Abstraction and fault-tolerance reports say whether the exact or the numeric path decided, and a numeric report names its norm. No numeric verdict passes for exact.',
    out: `composition law in frobenius-on-choi: ε ≤ ‖τ₂‖_post · ε₁ + ‖τ₁‖_pre · ε₂ over 1 queries, holds`,
  },
  {
    kind: 'Refusal',
    title: 'It refuses what it cannot decide.',
    text: 'A cyclic structure, a gate across code blocks, a non-commuting pair on a model and a numeric evaluation over its size cap each fail with an error that names the cause.',
    out: `refused: Calculation Error: Cz { control: 0, target: 2 } acts across outer blocks 0 and 1; a transversal gadget between code blocks is not part of this construction`,
  },
];
---
<ul class="rows">
  {props.map((p, i) => <OutputCard {...p} index={i} />)}
</ul>
<div class="also">
  <p>
    Four of the five tolerance types derive from the working real type’s machine epsilon, so
    switching <code>f64</code> to <code>f32</code> moves them; shot noise derives from the shot
    count.
  </p>
  <p>
    A candidate that names a causal structure reaches the experiment stage only through
    validation: a plant configured with structural candidates has no <code>control</code>
    implementation, so the compiler rejects the call.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .rows {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  @media (min-width: 800px) { .rows { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }

  .also { display: grid; gap: var(--space-3); max-width: var(--measure); }
  .also p { margin: 0; color: var(--fg-1); font-size: var(--t-body-sm); }
</style>
